# PAIRING

## Pair models
- Driver and passenger, actor and coach, user advocate, adversarial review
- Modes: stop hook handoff, inline steering, sequential context, explicit tool
- Targets: shallow solutions, forgotten instructions, review-and-commit workflows

## Council
- Parallel prompt to several models, one summarizes

# TOOLS

## Strict tools
- Reason required per change, across shell, write, and edit
- Reports diff and LOC change
- UIs render the reason as a prominent part of the diff

## Subagent edit review
- Edit tools dispatch a separate model to review the proposed change
- Pass or fail with reason

# GATES

## Dev-loop gates
- Agent cannot write until it passes entry gates, cannot finish until it passes exit gates
- Which gates apply and when is an open question
- Stop gate: reviewer returns pass or fail with reason, minimal version
- Per-tool-call gate: reviewer catches mistakes early, expensive
- Plan-before-write gate: exit tools locked each turn until a proposal tool call unlocks them
- Could combine with the stop gate
- Candidate use for Jev / decision models

